<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 390 0 R
/E ( The World Wild Fund for Nature \(WWF\) is one of the largest international nature conservation nonprofit organizations, founded in the Swiss Confederation more than 50 years ago on April 29 of 1961, under the idea of building a future in which humans live in harmony with nature, through sustaining the natural world. Since its foundation, WWF has invested around 10 billion dollars in more than 13,000 projects seeking to protect and restore natural habitats, stop the mass extinction of wildlife, and make the production and consumption more sustainable. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
536 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 390 0 R
/E ( WWF emerged with a small group of enthusiasts and committed naturalists who shared one interest: nature. During the decade of the 60s, it contributed to many species and habitat conservation projects around the world. It later strengthened its commitment to international treaties related to the environment, expanding its focus to more areas related to wildlife, water and nature. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
537 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 390 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
538 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 390 0 R
/E ( WWF is recognized as one of the most respected independent conservation organizations in the world, maintaining its independence and with all their actions determined exclusively by the organization. The organization receives funding from both public and private donors, it also works with governments and private organizations in order to achieve their goals and fulfill their projects. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
