/P 392 0 R
/E ( The organization has led pioneering projects such as the first eco-labels of consumption and the promotion of international agreements on wetlands,wildlife trade,biodiversity and climate change. Today, with presence in nearly 100 countries and the support of more than 35 million people. WWF is a global multicultural network that combines international leadership with local action, working to build a fairer, healthier and more sustainable world for both the planet and humanity. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
561 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 392 0 R
/E (Documents )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
562 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 392 0 R
/E ( As previously mentioned, the WWF is not a government organization or a political body like the UN. Therefore, it does not issue binding resolutions, treaties or law instruments. It produces a varied catalog of reports, policy briefs and campaign material for the public. Among its most influential contributions are their flagship reports, major publications that compile critical data and guide international discussions and policymaking. Most notoriously, it publishes the biennial Living Planet Report, a document describing current trends in global health and biodiversity. The main objective of this report, along with most of its other works, is to highlight threats to the natural world and influencing governments, international bodies, businesses, and the general public.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
