705 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 403 0 R
/T (Actions to Safeguard Genetic Diversity and Ensure Equitable Access to Genetic Resources, Addressing the Accelerating Loss of Ecological Variety)
/E (Actions to Safeguard Genetic Diversity and Ensure Equitable Access to Genetic Resources, Addressing the Accelerating Loss of Ecological Variety)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
706 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 403 0 R
/E ( Genetic diversity is the foundation of life on Earth, however, it is disappearing at an alarming rate as climate change, deforestation, industrialization and overexploitation intensify. It is estimated that there has been a 73% decline in the average size of monitored wildlife populations in just 50 years. Besides, over one million species are currently at risk of extinction. When a species disappears, its unique genetic information is lost forever, with no chances of recovering it and weakening entire ecosystems around the world. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
707 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 403 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
708 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 403 0 R
/E ( This topic addresses two urgent challenges: protecting genetic diversity from rapid ecological loss and ensuring equitable access to genetic resources from those species for all nations. Safeguarding genetic variety is essential not only for environmental stability, but also for global food security, public health, sustainable development and, with an ethical biotechnologic and scientific approach, a future restoration of those genetically preserved species. All of these while regulating equitable access to genetic resources of all species for every country and preventing biopiracy.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
709 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 403 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
