>>
endobj
731 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 405 0 R
/E ( A global analysis published in the journal Nature has analyzed more than 30 years of data on the genetics of 628 species of animals, plants, fungi, and other organisms, and has found that approximately two out of three populations have lost genetic diversity during this period.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
732 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 405 0 R
/E ( This loss of diversity can be observed not only in endangered species, but also in those that are not currently considered as such, indicating the existence of a widespread phenomenon among all wildlife.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
