754 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 407 0 R
/E (In terms of food security, the FAO has promoted the Treaty, which aims to ensure the conservation and exchange of essential plant genetic resources. This treaty promotes a multilateral system of access to plant genetic resources that facilitates international cooperation and, at the same time, strengthens the resilience of agricultural systems to the effects of climate change.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
755 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 407 0 R
/E ( In addition, the FAO has implemented mechanisms for the protection of animal genetic diversity, such as the Domestic Animal Diversity Information System \(DAD-IS\), which provides information on the status of livestock breeds worldwide and assists decision-making in the field of in situ and ex situ conservation. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
756 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 407 0 R
/E ( Finally, the Kunming-Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework, agreed upon in 2022, symbolizes a renewed commitment to halting and reversing biodiversity loss by 2030. This framework contains clear objectives, such as the conservation of the genetic diversity of both wild and domesticated species and highlights the role of international cooperation as the driving force behind the achievement of these objectives. WWF, for example, has adopted these goals within conservation projects, scientific research, and work with local communities in order to strengthen efforts for global biodiversity governance.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
757 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 407 0 R
/T (Current Situation)
/E (Current Situation)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
758 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 407 0 R
/E ( 2020s. Scientific assessments conducted under the Intergovernmental Science-Policy Platform on Biodiversity and Ecosystem Services \(IPBES\) have confirmed that genetic diversity is declining across species at an unprecedented rate, undermining ecosystem resilience, food security, and the capacity of societies to adapt to climate change.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
759 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 407 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
760 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 407 0 R
/E (In parallel, the implementation of the Nagoya Protocol continues to be a central issue in international negotiations. Since its entry into force in 2014, Parties have met regularly through the Meetings of the Parties to the Nagoya Protocol \(COP-MOP\) to address challenges related to access and benefit-sharing \(ABS\). Recent discussions, particularly between 2020 and 2024, have focused on improving compliance mechanisms and addressing gaps that disadvantage biodiversity-rich developing countries and Indigenous peoples.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
