<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E (Conservation of Genetic Diversity)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
779 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E ( This pillar is focused on preventing the extinction of species and the erosion of genetic diversity within populations around the world. The protection of habitats needs to be addressed in order to create a discussion around other subtopics.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
780 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E (Equitable Access and Sharing)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
781 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E ( Fair access to genetic resources for ethical uses is highly relevant to avoid monopolies or biopiracy. Each Member State should make sure of the implementation of treaties, protocols or laws, such as the Nagoya Protocol, to ensure that every community benefits from the use of biodiversity, guaranteeing transparency, consent and no possibility of patents.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
782 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E (Sustainable Use of Genetic Resources)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
783 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E ( It is crucial to prevent the exploitation of species and their genetic information for either commercial or scientific purposes. The regulation of genetic resources through the balancing between economic funding with long-term ecosystem resilience leads to the avoidance of a possible depletion of them. )
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
