3634 0 obj
<<
/Title (The previously mentioned information from 2015 and 2021, also suggests that wildlife crime is not isolated to distinct regions. Instead, it has evolved over time into a widely distributed system. It operates across a wide range of countries and territories. This geographic spread also implies a level of adaptation: trafficking networks can shift routes, exploit jurisdictional gaps, and move activity across borders to reduce the risk of detection. As operations diversify across species, products, and transit points, enforcement becomes more complex. This makes coordinated, international responses even more necessary.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3630 0 R
/Next 3638 0 R
>>
endobj
