/Title (In conclusion, the current situation reflects both progress and persistent challenges. International organizations, treaties, and conferences have established a robust institutional architecture to address genetic diversity loss, particularly since 2022. However, accelerating ecological pressures, unresolved issues such as DSI, and persistent inequalities in access and benefit-sharing continue to limit the effectiveness of global action. Addressing these challenges will require sustained political commitment, enhanced international cooperation, and adequate financing to translate global agreements into meaningful outcomes on the ground.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 3649 0 R
/Next 3645 0 R
>>
