/Title (One of the most complex and ongoing debates concerns Digital Sequence Information \(DSI\). As genomic technologies advanced rapidly during the 2010s and 2020s, genetic data increasingly became accessible through digital databases without the physical transfer of biological material. This issue gained prominence during CBD COP15 \(2022\), where Parties agreed to continue negotiations on a multilateral benefit-sharing mechanism for DSI. Further technical and political discussions have since taken place in intersessional working groups and at subsidiary body meetings under the CBD, highlighting the evolving nature of genetic resource governance.)
